# Issue description\n\nThere are some issues in the api.json in the godot_headers repo for 3.6.2.\nI was going to make a pull request on that repo but then reading the docs it sent me over here.\nsee https://github.com/godotengine/godot-headers/issues/99\nHowever having 3.6.2 tag checked out in my local godot repo I can't find the corresponding api.json file\n\nI'm working in Haskell with some bindings for godot 3 which I've just brought up to date for the LTS version and ran into this issue as I'm trying to setup a project which uses a subrepo and my changes to fix the issues (the api.json is used for code-gen) are just local to the subrepo so I'm probably going to have to fork temporarily but ideally I'd fix them for other people too.  \n\nIf you can advise on how to modify the api.json for 3.6, that'd be good, or how I can communicate what the problems are.  I actually wonder if it might be easiest to just open a pull request on the other repo just so you can see what I'm talking about.  Effectively there are 2 types of errors:\n* things that should be `Material` but claim to be one of multiple concrete materials (eg \"type\": \"ShaderMaterial, ParticlesMaterial\") - approx 10 of these\n* things that claim to have type Object but really should have something more specific - eg mesh should have type ArrayMesh and not Object.  There's about 5 of those\n\nCheers\n\nJonny\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122396/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122396/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}